        56.66524124145508,
        168.63714599609375,
        65.8308334350586
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "An alternative to the MMH algorithm to sample from p.θ,x1:T |y1:T / consists of using the Gibbs",
      "bbox": [
        42.70989990234375,
        67.88313293457031,
        438.2303771972656,
        79.49478149414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sampler which samples iteratively from p.θ|y1:T , x1:T / and pθ.x1:T |y1:T /. It is often possible to",
      "bbox": [
        42.710174560546875,
        79.83833312988281,
        438.2276916503906,
        91.5595703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sample from p.θ|y1:T , x1:T / and thus the potentially tedious design of a proposal density for θ",
